    "body": "Pushed 5aca9dcb (merged upstream/main, then the test commit).\n\n1. Posting MCP test: `a_setups_own_post_picked_over_mcp_reaches_its_own_posted_file_and_undoes` (`mcp_setup_mount_trace.rs`). Setup1 gets `Siemens 840D`, Setup2 `Haas` via `set_setup_post`; `post` writes two files; file 1 is Siemens dialect (`; VMC 3-AXIS`, `N10 G17 G710`, Face1 only, no M30), file 2 is Haas (`%` / `(VMC 3-AXIS)`, Face2, G55, no G710). Then `undo` (the session history also holds the generate step, so it undoes until Setup2's own post is null, bounded at 4) and re-post: Setup1's file is byte-identical, Setup2's file is the document's Fanuc (`%\\nO0001 (VMC 3-AXIS)`) again.\n2. Machine-kind: `a_post_that_does_not_serve_the_setups_machine_is_accepted_then_refused_at_post`. The `Fanuc Lathe` post on a milling setup is accepted by `set_setup_post` (`own_post: true`); `post` then refuses (isError) naming Face2 and the lathe post (#1213's wording), and nothing is written.\n\nGate: quick (lib + mcp_edit_machine, mcp_holder, mcp_setup, mcp_setup_mount_trace, mcp_verify) green; clippy -D warnings clean. The skill-row note is left to the follow-up issue.\n\nReady for a re-review.",
