    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 5aca9dcb7b161e5712c06d4424a73fb625ead5a1 -->\n**Delta review (M3) of the review at 193f6304: ready for the maintainer to merge. Both requested changes are done.**\n\n**Requested change 1, the posting leg:** `crates/app/tests/mcp_setup_mount_trace.rs:151`.\n- Two setups get Siemens 840D and Haas through `set_setup_post`, and `post` writes one file per mount, each with its own dialect markers.\n- After the `undo`, Setup1 keeps its post and its file is byte-identical, and Setup2 follows the document's Fanuc again.\n\n**Requested change 2, the machine-kind pin:** the same file, line 187. `set_setup_post` accepts the lathe post, `post` then refuses it, naming the lathe post and Face2, and nothing is written.\n\n**Same command as the Setup pane:** `set_setup_post` (`crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs:178`) runs `SetSetupPost` through the session History as one undo step. Bad input is refused by name, and there is no unwrap or panic.\n\n**Local results,** merged with current main (clean):\n- `mcp_setup` 8, `mcp_setup_mount_trace` 3, `mcp` 18, `mcp_holder` 5, `mcp_verify` 3, `mcp_edit_machine` 3, `setup_mounts_post` 8, `setup_mount_trace` 6;\n- clippy is clean.\n\n**Notes, not blocking:**\n- The camcraft-mcp skill row for `set_setup_post` is still owed. It is a process file, so it needs a PROCESS_VERSION above main's; #960 holds 36. Please name its follow-up issue in the body.\n- A `.cps` path through the tool is untested.\n",
